title: _request hands a bare JSON scalar body back undecoded
updated: 2026-08-27T06:35:42Z
---

Role::HTTP::_request only decodes a body that matches /^\s*[\{\[]/, so a response whose whole payload is a JSON scalar -- null, true, false, a number, a quoted string -- is returned as its raw bytes instead of the decoded value.

Found while implementing /plugins (karr #28). GET /plugins/privileges answers a bare `null` for a plugin that demands no privileges: moby's computePrivileges starts from `var privileges types.PluginPrivileges` and appends only what the plugin config asks for, so a nil Go slice reaches the wire. The caller then gets the four-character string 'null' where an ArrayRef is documented -- and in that endpoint's case would POST it straight back to /plugins/pull as a JSON string where the engine expects an array.

API::Docker::API::Plugins::privileges guards against it locally (`return [] unless ref $result eq 'ARRAY'`), with a comment and a regression test in t/plugins.t ('privileges: a plugin that demands nothing answers null'), which also pins the transport's current behaviour so a fix here shows up there.

Any other endpoint with a nil-able Go slice or pointer as its whole response body has the same problem. Deciding whether _request should decode a scalar body is a transport-wide return-shape question, which is why it was not fixed in passing.
